+  // Apostate: V8 sizes its heap from installed memory, and the resulting
+  // ceiling is readable from JavaScript as performance.memory.jsHeapSizeLimit
+  // and console.memory.jsHeapSizeLimit. Left on the host's figure it is a
+  // second, unspoofed readout of the fact navigator.deviceMemory reports, and
+  // the two can contradict each other: V8's old generation is the installed
+  // memory halved and then clamped to 4 GiB, so a host under 8 GiB emits a
+  // limit no device with the claimed memory would emit. Measured on this
+  // build, a 36 GiB host reports 4395630592 bytes for every profile in the
+  // current pool, which is why the contradiction is invisible here and would
+  // appear immediately on a 2 or 4 GiB VM - the machines this browser is
+  // actually run on.
+  //
+  // Supply the claimed figure and let V8 do its own arithmetic, for the same
+  // reason patch 0006 supplies the input to ApproximatedDeviceMemory rather
+  // than overriding its output: the mapping from memory to heap limit is
+  // V8's, it is coarse and quantised, and reimplementing it here would drift
+  // and eventually emit a number no Chrome produces.
+  //
+  // Capacity is only ever reduced, matching the clamp in patches 0004 and
+  // 0006. The claim is therefore always at or below what the host can back, so
+  // the heap genuinely behaves the way the reported limit says it does, and
+  // the browser gives up earlier than stock rather than later. Virtual memory
+  // stays the host's; it is not part of the claim.
+  const base::apostate::Profile* profile = base::apostate::Profile::Get();
+  const std::optional<uint64_t> claimed_memory =
+      profile ? profile->memory_total_bytes() : std::nullopt;
+  const uint64_t host_memory =
+      base::SysInfo::AmountOfTotalPhysicalMemory().InBytes();
   params->constraints.ConfigureDefaults(
-      base::SysInfo::AmountOfTotalPhysicalMemory().InBytes(),
+      claimed_memory.has_value() ? std::min(*claimed_memory, host_memory)
+                                 : host_memory,
       base::SysInfo::AmountOfVirtualMemory().InBytes());
